hi|n|A coming to, or near approach; admittance; admission; accessibility; as, to gain access to a prince. ; The means, place, or way by which a thing may be approached; passage way; as, the access is by a neck of land. ; Admission to sexual intercourse. ; Increase by something added; addition; as, an access of territory. [In this sense accession is more generally used.] ; An onset, attack, or fit of disease. ; A paroxysm; a fit of passion; an outburst; as, an access of fury.	a:p5p,64,5;1l3g,51,4;1e3p,51,321;10mg,50,6;1pf5,49,18;125u,47,27;1qzd,44,6;25mz,41,3;1loa,40,2;1pzv,39,4~1e3p,51,321;13x9,8,30;125u,47,27;15ne,25,27;1imv,31,22;1pf5,49,18;1mo0,13,15;t96,13,14;167n,15,8;kcb,12,8	v:1pzw,54,4;1pzu,48,7;1loa,46,3;vn9,42,5;27xf,42,3;1tbe,41,6;iyt,38,3;tx0,37,5;1dhn,35,10;167r,34,4~mu8,33,40;1mfd,15,21;28l,19,12;16vu,29,11;vn4,13,10;1dhn,35,10;1pzu,48,7;1mfe,14,6;1tbe,41,6;uuq,6,6	V:17sg,4,3~17sg,4,3	n:1610,36,22;21e8,34,4;uup,15,7;1cbv,13,4;htb,1,14~1610,36,22;htb,1,14;uup,15,7;1cbv,13,4;21e8,34,4	N:17t7,60,4;1pzx,38,3;1pn4,36,11;1jyj,33,21;yjm,33,3;1b56,29,7;1moa,26,12;ras,20,5;1e9k,20,21;161e,20,6~1mo2,12,21;1e9k,20,21;1jyj,33,21;273t,9,13;1moa,26,12;1mob,10,11;1pn4,36,11;1jyl,12,10;4qw,2,8;fdl,10,7
