vo|v|To move to action; to actuate; to animate. ; To perform; to execute; to do. ; To perform, as an actor; to represent dramatically on the stage. ; To assume the office or character of; to play; to personate; as, to act the hero. ; To feign or counterfeit; to simulate. ; To exert power; to produce an effect; as, the stomach acts upon food. ; To perform actions; to fulfill functions; to put forth energy; to move, as opposed to remaining at rest; to carry into effect a determination of the will. ; To behave or conduct, as in morals, private duties, or public offices; to bear or deport one's self; as, we know not why he has acted so. ; To perform on the stage; to represent a character.	o:22xr,15,4~22xr,15,4	d:1w23,11,5;ugr,2,3;x5,2,7;2fi,1,5~x5,2,7;1w23,11,5;2fi,1,5;ugr,2,3	D:ycx,88,3;201s,84,4;kwe,81,4;1o66,72,4;k9,44,5;45q,43,4;1lun,43,3;pk4,39,4;1urt,37,4;1oc5,24,4~k9,44,5;45q,43,4;201s,84,4;1oc5,24,4;1urt,37,4;qw7,16,4;1o66,72,4;kwe,81,4;pk4,39,4;ycx,88,3
